  "toyota_summary": "The Irish EU presidency proposed a compromise on automotive emissions rules that would tighten the 2035 carbon-reduction target beyond what was previously negotiated. The specific threshold wasn't fully detailed in available reports, but the move signals movement toward stricter standards rather than looser ones as some manufacturers had hoped.\n\nAutomakers face real pressure now. Europe still sets the global tone for emissions regs—what passes here eventually shapes rules in other major markets. A tighter 2035 target means less time to phase out internal combustion engines and higher costs to meet standards faster.\n\nWatch whether major producing nations like Germany and France accept the Irish proposal or push back.",
